      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa has a yield strength of approximately 330 MPa at 1273 K.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa reaches approximately 423 MPa compressive strength at 30% strain at 1273 K.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 0.5 at.% Hf can be introduced as a minor alloying addition during melting and casting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514651::rubric_card::000::c489cb1ed6"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 0.5 at.% Hf to TiVNbTa will improve elevated-temperature strength retention.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf addition will promote fine, thermally stable precipitates or ordered phases in TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-induced features may form along or near grain boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf will segregate to TiVNbTa grain boundaries and/or form nanoscale particles.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-induced particles or ordered phases will pin grain boundaries and obstruct dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boundary pinning will reduce grain growth and delay grain-boundary sliding, dislocation recovery, and dislocation annihilation at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Suppressing these high-temperature deformation and recovery processes will maintain a higher yield strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, Hf-modified TiVNbTa is expected to exceed the baseline yield strength by more than 10%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-modified TiVNbTa is expected to retain ductility better than the baseline in compression or tension.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefit applies around 1273 K under mechanical loading, comparable strain rates, and controlled oxidation conditions.",
